<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >The term "Wicca" only refers to the modern schools of witchcraft founded by James Gardner(In England) and Raymond Buckland(in the USA).  There are many way older schools of Witchcraft who refer to themselves as witches, not Wicca.<br>
<br>
Oh, and as an interesting side note, do you know the last anti-witchcraft laws were not repealed in England till about 1950 or so.<br>
<br>
Oh, and for the record I am a practicing witch.  It is a great religion, having more to do with focusing on love and natural forces, than any specific rules.  In fact, the witches reed is An it harm none, do it.  Which loosely means, if it doesn't hurt anyone, including yourself, go right ahead and do it.<br>
<br>
Oh lets see, I can rant about this topic all day, so I'll stop here, but if you are interested in learning about the religion.  I suggest starting with "The Spiral Dance" by Starhawk and "The Complete Book of Witchcraft" By Ramond Buckland.<br>
<br>
</font></p>

