Now the church took a look at witchcraft and saw us doing bizarre things like jumping around on brooms to show our crops how high to grow(this is, incidently, where the myth of witches riding broomsticks comes from), and worshipping our horned god, and decided we must worship satan.<br>
<br>
After all our God has horns, Satan has horns, ergo our God must be Satan, which is absurd simply because Satan is an invention of the Christian faith.  They of course, ignored the fact completely that we worship a Goddess in equal measure.<br>
<br>
Hell, even worship is too strong a word, We respect and call aid from the Goddess and The God, but to say we worship implies they are beyond us, when in fact they are all around us.<br>
